          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ud",
          "text": "An experienced ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uf",
          "text": "personal injury lawyer in Thornton",
          "marks": [
            "l6ue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ug",
          "text": " can optimize your odds of securing financial compensation for a brain injury case with proven and aggressive legal strategies. Your attorney can investigate your accident, collect proof of fault, and go up against any defendant in pursuit of justice and a positive case outcome on your behalf.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6uj",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ui",
          "text": "Types of Brain Injuries",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ul",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6uk",
          "text": "The brain is a sensitive organ that is easily susceptible to serious injury. If the head or skull suffers a blow, bump or jolt in any kind of accident, it can negatively affect the brain’s functionality. This is what is known as a traumatic brain injury, or TBI. If the brain’s necessary blood or oxygen supply gets interrupted, this can cause an acquired brain injury or ABI. Some examples of brain injury types include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
