    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6v5",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6v4",
          "text": "The symptoms associated with a brain injury often include headaches, dizziness, and nausea. Moderate to severe head and brain injuries can lead to changes in behavioral patterns, confusion or disorientation, loss of consciousness, memory loss, coma, and death. Every head and brain injury should be taken seriously and treated by medical professionals.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6v7",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6v6",
          "text": "Common Causes of Brain Injuries",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6v9",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6v8",
          "text": "Many brain injuries in Colorado are avoidable. They stem from incidents such as a driver hitting a bicyclist or an anesthesiologist using too much anesthesia. In these scenarios, the brain injury survivor can file a lawsuit in pursuit of justice and financial compensation for related losses against the at-fault party. A brain injury lawsuit can arise from many different preventable accidents in Thornton, including:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
